Expected elements: present

Presence: exit `← demo` → `/demo` (x24-75, #4F46E5); `.dbgid` `0xb63616…6359`; `Partial`; `block 101`; eight stepping controls; `128 / 1,315`; phase rail live on `FETCHING`; DATA is the first row of the transaction pane with the `Synthetic demo data` badge and its own sentences; no band above the bar; four panes intact. FOCUSED CONTROL FOUND: x81-197 y17-45. Must-not-show all clear, and provably: this PNG differs from `debugger__wide__light.png` in exactly 29 rows, all of them the ring. Zero reflow, zero `.copied`.

Central question — no, it does not read as a button; it reads as a focused text field. Because the diff is ring-only, hydration changed no glyph: same mono, 8.5px advance, 10px band, #101010. Type contributes nothing. The one drawn signal is the product's own `:focus-visible` token, and it is square (radius 0) with 2px horizontal inset, in a bar where every chip and badge is radius 3-7px with 10px inset. Resting state — what everyone actually sees — is a bare value.

Instrument correction: the block's "UA focus ring / the design system does not choose" is wrong (`styles.nim:114`, tokenised, #3B82F6 → #60A5FA), and "plain-build views show no rail" is wrong. That is why my central finding is P2, not P1.

Fix: one `.copybtn` rule — `cursor:copy`, the `.copyable` hover surface, `border-radius:var(--bt-radius-xs)`. And `.copied`/`.copyfailed` still draw nothing on click.

Rating: 6/10

